lmmse_shim.hpp supplies the minimal array/LUT/math/host interface, scalar
execution and gamma functions from rtengine/color.h gamma24_17/igamma24_17,
tables from rtengine/color.cc, and floating lookup semantics from rtengine/LUT.h
at the same commit. It contains no GUI, threading or SSE dependency.
lmmse_demosaic.py strips dependency includes at build time and replaces final
nonnegative floors with a switchable signed floor. Its signed mode disables
the original unit-interval and difference-domain gates, extends the gamma
linear toe below zero and uses the analytic gamma pair above white (avoiding
a finite-LUT extrapolation round-trip bias). Stock mode keeps upstream gates.
Core directional interpolation, 9-tap low-pass, nine-sample MMSE, chroma
reconstruction, median iterations and optional edge reinforcement are retained.
The primary candidate fixes iterations=3 (gamma plus two median passes).
Iterations 5..8 require whole-image mode because edge reinforcement is in-place.
This is not a claim of complete RawTherapee application or CPU/SIMD equivalence.
IGV, in rtengine/demosaic_algos.cc, was inspected but not ported/tested.
No non-commercial code, pretrained weights or original photographs are included.
